  GOAL
  Demonstrate a LOCAL end-to-end proof of concept where a Spring Boot "SIFFT config web
  service" (already present on this machine at Desktop\sifft-config-api) serves ingestion
  configuration over REST, and a Python driver consumes that configuration over HTTP to
  drive the installed SIFFT library to ingest files into Delta tables on the local
  filesystem. No Databricks, no cloud. REDUCED-FUNCTIONALITY PoC: delimited CSV/pipe files
  only, format=delta, write modes overwrite/append, schema modes overwrite/merge.

  ARCHITECTURE (what we are proving)
    Spring Boot web service (localhost:8080)                 SIFFT library (local Spark)
      GET /api/v1/read-configs   ─┐
      GET /api/v1/write-configs  ─┘──▶ Python driver (HTTP) ──▶ process_file(...)   read+parse
                                                             ──▶ df.toDF(*columns)   apply cols
                                                             ──▶ write_table(...)    write Delta
                                                             ──▶ Delta tables on disk

  VERIFIED FACTS about the installed package `sifft` 0.9.3 (do NOT "correct" these):
  - There is NO `import sifft`. Installing sifft places TOP-LEVEL modules in the env:
    file_processing, table_writing, dataframe_validation, file_management.
    Import directly:
        from file_processing import process_file
        from table_writing import write_table, TableWriteOptions
  - Verified signatures:
        process_file(file_path, spark, read_options=None, metadata_path=None,
                     raise_on_error=False, tracking=None, tracking_location=None,
                     storage_options=None) -> FileProcessingResult
            (result attrs include: success, dataframe, rows_processed, message)
        write_table(df, table_name, spark, options=None, source_file_path=None,
                    file_size=None, raise_on_error=False) -> TableWriteResult
            (result attrs include: success, rows_written, error)
        TableWriteOptions(format='delta', mode='append', partition_by=None,
                          schema_mode='strict', merge_keys=None, create_if_not_exists=True,
                          add_source_metadata=False, source_metadata_columns=None,
                          extra_metadata=None)
  - Apply config column names with:  df = result.dataframe.toDF(*columns)
  - Write a path-based Delta table (no metastore needed) using table_name of the form:
        delta.`C:/forward/slash/path`     (backticks required; forward slashes)

